course: dictionary
lesson: 3325
title: Even: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word even can mean different things, so context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it. In «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air, so even a small rise warms the planet», even means that a small rise matters too, not just a big one.
explain: In maths and games, even means equal or split fairly. Four is an even number because it splits into two equal groups with none left over. If the score is even, both sides have the same points. To break even means you neither make a profit nor lose money.
explain: Even can also mean flat, smooth and level, as in an even floor. Even out and even up mean to make things equal. When you are not sure which meaning fits, put your choice into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Even can join other words too. «Even if» and «even though» both mean although. «Even though it was raining, we played outside» tells you the rain did not stop the game.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and it is your best clue to which meaning of even you need.
fact: Even numbers end in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8, and they can be split into two equal groups.
fact: «Even» can mean flat, smooth and level, as in an even floor.
fact: «Even» can add stress to something surprising, as in «Super glue can even glue eyelids».
fact: «Even if» and «even though» mean although, and «break even» means no profit and no loss.
exercise: «Super glue can even glue eyelids, so only an adult uses it.» What does even add to this sentence? | It shows the number of glue tubes | *It adds surprise: gluing eyelids is something you would not expect | It means the glue is equal to water | It makes the sentence about flat ground
exercise: Which of these is an even number? | *12 | 7 | 15 | 9
exercise: «The score is even with two minutes left.» What does even mean here? | One team has no points | The game has already finished | The pitch is flat and smooth | *Both teams have the same points
test: «Even Jake admitted he was wrong.» What does even add to this sentence? | It means flat and level | It means a number split in two | It means the two sides are equal | *It adds surprise: Jake is someone you would not expect to say that
test: Which phrase means although? | even out | break even | an even floor | *even though
exam: «The potoo sits still, and even with its eyes shut it can see through notches in its eyelids.» What does even mean here? | It means a number that can be split in two | *It adds surprise: this is unexpected, even with its eyes shut | It means flat and smooth | It means equal in score
